{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55625-edge-cases-strix-attack","id":55625,"title":"Edge Cases : Strix Attack!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-22T12:52:26-08:00","id":55625,"title":"Edge Cases : Strix Attack!","content":"So, let's propose a Strix... from Requiem... decides it wants to claim a Demon as a host, without knowing who/what the demon is.<br /> <br /> So! Let's examine the outcome!<br /> <br /> SPOOF : Can 'spoofing' a Strix in such a situation work? Spoof reads that it can be used on any power that reveals the Demon as supernatural by implication. Strix are able to recall the memories of the host with a successful roll. Accordingly, I have treated this as a sort of 'mind reading' power that can therefore be spoofed, although this form of mind-reading also has the rather convenient side effect of body thievery.<br /> <br /> COVER : Can the Demon 'change cover' outside of the Strix's knowledge to confuse / baffle it? I've ruled no. The character in question has an interlock called 'Code and Cup Game' that allows her to kinda teleport to wherever her Cover should be in order to shift covers - if you've played GTAV, imagine it working like character switching in that game. I've ruled that the Demon CANNOT use any active / conscious power because she is subdued, for now.<br /> <br /> 'SOMETHING OFF' : What capacity would a Strix have for determining a Cover it had just possessed was unusual, besides obvious reality relics like brand names that don't exist being in her cupboard?<br /> <br /> I've currently determined that the Strix believes it has claimed a normal human being ; when it examined the memories of the human, it was spoofed so it instead came up with vast regions of inexplicable 'lost time' from periods when the Cover wasn't being used. Considering the Strix is trying to track down a Julii host that was stolen from it, it seems intuitive to suggest the Strix now believes the Demon is in fact a Dominated mortal who is being used as a pawn by some sort of Kindred enemy to steal her toys.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Criticism?<br /> <br /> Also, since I kicked this thread off, anybody got fun ideas for what'd happen if a Strix used 'Synthesis' in a human host? Not that this is planned, just idly pondering.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:01:55-08:00","id":55636,"title":"","content":"I don't know enough about the Strix to comment too heavily, but the Demon book does explain that &quot;Demon&quot;, like other splats, is a closed system. So while a Strix may notice something is 'odd' about a given character, without IC knowledge or justification it will never think, 'This is a damn Demon!!!11&quot;. As for spoofing, Cover is as much metaphysical protection (Spoofing, Supernatural Tolerance, etc.) as it is physical state of being. Cover is self-replicating code with varied levels of strength. If a Demon successfully spoofs, the Cover rating would adapt to the new perspective being applied to it (the Strix's supernatural perspective), going in-depth enough to provide topical answers to subjective insight as necessary. Same as if a Mortal were investigating. The question then becomes to what degree the Strix would be concerned about gaps. <br /> <br /> Does OwlBoy really care that DemonJohnny didn't have a meaningful High School friend until 8 days before his graduation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:43:09-08:00","id":56707,"title":"","content":"Cool idea. Depending on how powerful and smart the strix is it might be cool if it accidentally switched covers. It might not even notice at first, its detached enough from its hosts that massive changes are ignored. Then it wonders why everyone is staring lol. Or a more hedonistic strix might have a grand old time changing covers and freaking out passerby's.<br /> <br /> For synthesis I'm thinking it could give permanent undead themed glitches and a bonus on compromise roles as the demon is less angel like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T11:03:07-08:00","id":57521,"title":"","content":"Okay! Some thoughts!<br /> <br /> No, spoofing won't protect the Demon. But their immunity to mind reading and ability to lie flawlessly will. Demons are awesome at hiding and lying. They have no natural immunity to being mind controlled or possessed, but they would be able to determine what their body is thinking at any given time. To do otherwise kind of undermines the whole idea of the demon's innate resistance to mind reading or lying. Now, a demon that doesn't offer the strix anything from its mind is likely going to be considered to be breaking Cover. And that's bad. But it could feed it thoughts. Maybe even trick it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I agree that, while possessed by a strix, the demon has no control over his supernatural powers, including ability to swap Covers or burn one to the ground; I'd allow spoofing, since that's reflexive and doesn't require conscious thought. If something -could- force a new cover, I'd say the Strix gets put into storage with the bad Cover. And, if the demon wrested control long enough to go loud? *soft whistle* Poor little shadow. I wonder if Pacts could swap possession between hosts? <br /> <br /> <br /> How would a Strix determine something was off about the Cover? Same way as anyone else. Details not adding up. The demon (ie the memories it supplies) not cooperating, or suddenly remembering things the strix was sure wasn't there. That said, its a rare strix that understands or cares enough about people to actually bother looking at the details long or hard enough. In terms of powers? Synthesis could be a flag, considering that I don't think its possible by the rules. The whole no-template-stacking . If, however, you allowed it? Ohhhhhh boy. A vampire demon. See below*<br /> <br /> <br /> So far, I think its good. The problem comes with the fact that the Cover is now acting out of character. Its going to be degrading, and fast! I would be calling for compromise rolls here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Okay! A vampire demon. I'm not a fan of mixing different rule sets here, but, thematically... well, this is what bloodlines are for in Vampire, and all the customization is for in Demon. If you use the demon rules, then make Glitches like sunlight/fire allergies, need to drink blood, etc. I'd reset any cipher progress the demon made, and force the keys/interlocks to mimic vampire qualities such as sympathetic connections, vinculum, and getting aether from blood. Using vampire, I'd make a daeva bloodline that granted demon abilities like spoofing, and an affinity for obfuscate that changed your appearance in a way that wasn't just illusion/mind control. That's a start, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T13:03:48-08:00","id":57583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55625-edge-cases-strix-attack?p=57521#post57521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, spoofing won't protect the Demon. But their immunity to mind reading and ability to lie flawlessly will. Demons are awesome at hiding and lying. They have no natural immunity to being mind controlled or possessed, but they would be able to determine what their body is thinking at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ended up ruling that to be entirely fair to the Strix ability, the Demon would not in fact be able to be 'awake' in any sort of meaningful sense during possession. This kinda sucks but demons aren't unique in WoD for being screwed if they are inhabited by a Strix. Everybody gets the same deal it seems; once it gets inside you, you are screwed until it leaves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55625-edge-cases-strix-attack?p=57521#post57521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To do otherwise kind of undermines the whole idea of the demon's innate resistance to mind reading or lying. Now, a demon that doesn't offer the strix anything from its mind is likely going to be considered to be breaking Cover. And that's bad. But it could feed it thoughts. Maybe even trick it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering I ruled that the demon had no real awareness with which to decieve the Strix and spoofed only as a reflexive action associated with Cover, the Demon does in fact have large 'blank areas'... but in the WoD, I don't consider these cover breaking. Large numbers of people experience 'Lost Time' on a semi-regular basis. It's not COMMON, by any stretch of the imagination, but it's not so rare as to be unusual.<br /> <br /> In this case, given that the Strix had reason to believe the Demon was a typical mortal pawn of the Kindred, it seems obvious that the cause of the lost time is -clearly- aggressive Domination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55625-edge-cases-strix-attack?p=57521#post57521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a Strix determine something was off about the Cover? Same way as anyone else. Details not adding up.</div> </div> </div> </div>This did, to some extent, happen - but the Cover was a patchwork cover of high rating so it was relatively secure. The Strix is not particularly inclined to Investigation so might be correctly accused of being a bit naive about such things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/55625-edge-cases-strix-attack?p=57521#post57521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The demon (ie the memories it supplies) not cooperating, or suddenly remembering things the strix was sure wasn't there. That said, its a rare strix that understands or cares enough about people to actually bother looking at the details long or hard enough. In terms of powers? Synthesis could be a flag, considering that I don't think its possible by the rules. The whole no-template-stacking . If, however, you allowed it? Ohhhhhh boy. A vampire demon. See below*</div> </div> </div> </div>This ended up never being an issue, but I was fond of the idea of suggesting that this might create a VII vampire, as per the 'God Machine Slaves' suggestion of what the VII could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}